WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.900
Ola is at home with her cat.

2
00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.050
Mam kota.

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.800
There is no word for a. Just: cat.

4
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:13.590
Kot śpi.

5
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:20.820
And no word for the. She means her cat, so in English: the cat.

6
00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:23.730
Mam psa.

7
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:30.380
In the park, Ola sees a cat she does not know.

8
00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.470
Kot śpi.

9
00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:38.820
The same words. Here, in English: a cat is sleeping.

10
00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:47.610
Polish has no articles: no separate words for a, an or the.

11
00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:52.370
At home, she means her cat: the cat is sleeping.

12
00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:57.120
In the park, any cat: a cat is sleeping.

13
00:00:57.470 --> 00:01:04.630
When you translate into English, choose a, an or the from the context.

14
00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:12.470
Ola talks about her pet. I have a dog. What does she say?

15
00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:17.130
Mam psa.

16
00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:21.490
Did you say it? Say it once more, out loud.

17
00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:24.450
Mam psa.

18
00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:30.450
What is the cat doing? Say it in Polish.

19
00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:35.190
Kot śpi.

20
00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:39.550
Did you say it? Say it once more, out loud.

21
00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:42.590
Kot śpi.

22
00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:48.670
Read the examples below the video at your own pace.
